Parity with the web source:
  - Props -> state: open->IsOpen, onClose->CloseRequested, title->Title, size->Size (sm|md|lg|full),
    children->Body, ariaLabel->AriaLabel.
  - Composition: acrylic scrim (TsMaterialOverlayBrush = --surface-overlay + backdrop-blur; opaque
    High-Contrast fallback = web forced-colors:bg-[Canvas]) under a centered surface
    (TsColorSurfaceBrush / TsColorBorderBrush / TsRadiusLg) with an OPTIONAL header (truncating
    SectionTitle title + 44x44 TsButton close "X" = web h-11 w-11 / WCAG 2.5.5) over a scrollable body.
    No footer command bar (the web Modal has none).
  - Behaviour: initial focus -> first focusable (FocusManager.FindFirstFocusableElement) else body; Esc
    closes; Tab / Shift+Tab trapped, wrapping first<->last (FindFirst/FindLastFocusableElement +
    InputKeyboardSource shift state); backdrop PointerPressed closes; focus restored to the opener
    (FocusManager.GetFocusedElement) on close; AutomationProperties.SetIsDialog + Name on the surface
    (web role="dialog" + aria-modal + aria-labelledby/aria-label).
  - Responsive (web < sm full-bleed / >= sm preset, max-h 90vh): ModalProjection.IsFullBleed /
    EffectiveMaxWidth / EffectiveMaxHeight (sm 384 / md 512 / lg 672 / full min(96vw,1100)).
  - States: the web Modal is a PURE presentational container with NO read query, so it has no
    loading / empty / error / stale / offline state. Its actual render branches are ALL reproduced:
    closed (renders nothing), open-with-title (header), open-without-title (ariaLabel), the four size
    presets, and the forced-colors / High-Contrast path. (Same honest accounting as the sibling
    AddAnnotationPopover, which likewise has no data states.)
  - i18n: the sole web string aria-label="Close" -> key common.close (catalog translation.common.close =
    "Close"); no English literal in native code; close button + dialog carry Narrator names.
  - Diagnostics (P1/S11): ModalDiagnostics emits "view.opened slug=Modal" on first show; PII-safe (title /
    body are never logged).
  - Motion: none (the web Modal has no transition) -> reduced-motion honoured by construction.

